<!--
  Categories as real publishers emit them, including the awkward parts.

  Item one carries six of them, which is what mostlylucid.net puts on every
  post, plus a domain attribute that is ignored, plus a spelling that differs
  only by case from one already present and a padded one that collapses onto
  another. Item two carries an empty element, a whitespace-only one, one over
  TagName.MaxLength and one with a comma: all four are refused, so it ends up
  with the single usable name.
-->
